export const instructions = "Create once or resume, then retain basis.sessionId and basis.viewId. Every reply is a version-2 DecisionFrame: basis holds the canonical turn and revision; control.gate says whether input is ready, awaiting an exact decision, recovering, lost ownership, ended or unavailable. outcome distinguishes accepted, rejected, unknown and notSubmitted input and reports actual actions and elapsed turns. scene.self contains position, location and vitals; scene.nearby, entities, features, map, inventory, here and perception describe the same perceived scene. events are fresh for this call. Use the returned frame directly for the next decision. Mutations require the exact observed viewId except create, resume, suspend, answer and cancel. Stale views reject without input. step {target:{direction}} attempts one adjacent ordinary move including tame-ally swaps; it refuses displayed non-allies. go {to} is destination-only travel; explore and descend are bounded legs. maxActions bounds actions and maxPlanningMs bounds planning (default 1000 ms). Read the reported stop and progress before continuing. run retains native direction, mode and noPickup behavior. Adjacent actions use target:{direction}, {position:{x,y}}, {ref}, or {symbol,scope:adjacent}; symbols must match uniquely, never choose a nearest match. inspect additionally permits direction self and symbol scope level. fire, throw and zap only accept target:{direction} with compass, self, up or down; omit target for an engine decision. Item actions use opaque itemId, never display names or slots. At gate decision use decision.reply with its exact decisionId and valueSchema, or decision.cancel when offered; do not replace questions or answer implicitly. Queries are free. syncState always includes full world and verifies retained uncertain receipts without replaying gameplay. Other scene replies are snapshots by default; includeWorld requests full world, and sinceViewId requests a delta against the last sent baseline, including in compact encoding. These options only control encoding. Historical receipt and query data live under result, never become a current scene or active question. RecoveryRequired blocks new input until verified; never blindly repeat an uncertain action or leg. Terminal details live in scene.end. An attempt is not a safety promise. suspend releases the saved run; quit asks to end it. help lists tools or one schema.";
